{"comments": "[{"path": "Checkpoints/github-master-kernel-8gates-live-20260922-233133/.githooks/pre-push", "existing_code": "# Correct approach: capture local_sha in the first pass.\nPUSHED_SHA=\"\"\nwhile read -r local_ref local_sha remote_ref _remote_sha; do\n  [ -z \"${local_ref:-}\" ] && continue\n  if [ \"$local_ref\" != \"DELETE\" ] && [ \"$local_ref\" != \"\" ]; then\n    PUSHED_SHA=\"${local_sha}\"\n    break\n  fi\ndone <<< \"$STDIN_LINES\"", "category": "bug", "severity": "high", "content": "New refs are never properly checked. On a first push of a new branch, there is no remote-tracking ref yet, so line 77 returns empty and the code falls to `git show --name-only` (line 85), which inspects only ONE commit instead of the full pushed range. Additionally, `break` (line 68) means only the first non-delete ref in a multi-ref push is captured. And `git for-each-ref refs/remotes/ | head -1` (line 77) picks an arbitrary remote-tracking branch that may not correspond to the push target, producing a meaningless diff range. Fix: follow the root .githooks/pre-push (2026-09-23) which loops ALL pushed refs from stdin, uses the per-ref <remote-sha>..<local-sha> range directly, handles all-zero remote-sha (new ref) by scanning `git ls-tree -r` at local_sha, and uses NUL-safe `while IFS= read -r` loops."},
        {"path": "Checkpoints/github-master-kernel-8gates-live-20260922-233133/.githooks/pre-push", "existing_code": "for f in $CHANGED_SRC; do", "category": "bug", "severity": "medium", "content": "Unquoted $CHANGED_SRC in `for f in $CHANGED_SRC` is subject to word-splitting and glob expansion. Filenames containing spaces (e.g. `src/my module.ts`) would be split into multiple iterations, causing false orphan detections or skipped files. Fix: use a NUL-safe loop: `while IFS= read -r f; do ... done <<< \"$CHANGED_SRC\"` as the root .githooks/pre-push does."},
